+# Taskboard CLI
+
+A dependency-free task manager written in TypeScript for [Bun](https://bun.sh/).
+Each invocation emits one JSON value. Data is stored in `.taskboard.json` in the
+current directory, or at the path in `TASKBOARD_FILE`.
+
+```sh
+bun run src/cli.ts add --title "Ship release" --tags work,urgent --due 2027-01-31
+bun run src/cli.ts list --status open --tag urgent
+bun run src/cli.ts list --overdue 2027-02-01
+bun run src/cli.ts done 1
+bun run src/cli.ts delete 1
+bun run src/cli.ts stats
+```
+
+Tags are trimmed, lowercased, and deduplicated. IDs increase monotonically and
+are not reused after deletion. Writes replace the database atomically using a
+temporary sibling file. Invalid commands, flags, dates, IDs, or database data
+produce a JSON error, write a diagnostic to stderr, and exit non-zero.
+
+Run the self-tests with:
+
+```sh
+bun test
+```
